% exp_id: 8b_cell_c_episode_v9d, 8b_v9d_ood_eval_v5
\end{table}

In this single-seed experiment, the episode-level fix appears more effective at 8B (90.3\% OOD vs.\ 17.2\% mean at 1.7B; Figure~\ref{fig:cross_scale}a), suggesting larger models may have more capacity unlocked by correct credit assignment.

\subsection{Cross-Environment Validation}
\label{sec:cross_env}

Step-independent training collapses on ScienceWorld~\cite{wang2022scienceworld} (30 task types, SFT baseline 30.1\% at $\tau{=}0.4$): Cell~A ($h{=}2$) drops to 0\% task success throughout all 15 steps, despite the higher baseline ($p{=}30.1\%$ vs.\ ALFWorld's $12.5\%$).% exp_id: scienceworld_grpo_cell_a, scienceworld_sft_eval_v2
Restricting context to $h{=}2$ drops SFT success from 34.8\% ($\tau{=}0$) to 4.5\% (30.3pp M1 gap), paralleling the 37.5pp gap at 8B ALFWorld (Figure~\ref{fig:cross_scale}b).% exp_id: sw_info_loss_bjb1
These single-seed results provide preliminary evidence that both mechanisms operate beyond ALFWorld; multi-seed and multi-environment verification would strengthen this claim.

\begin{figure*}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\textwidth]{fig_cross_scale.pdf}
\caption{(a)~Cross-scale verification (single seed): both collapse (Cell~A) and fix (Cell~D) are observed from 1.7B to 8B. The episode-level fix appears more effective at 8B (96.9\% vs.\ 34.4\% in-distribution). (b)~Information loss (M1) quantification (single seed each): restricting context to $h{=}2$ drops SFT performance by 37.5pp at 8B ALFWorld and 30.3pp on ScienceWorld.}
\label{fig:cross_scale}
\end{figure*}

